{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 (Understand) complete — root cause CONFIRMED at runtime\n\n### Step 0 — orientation\n- **0(a) duplicate found:** `cca6-3f7e-dd67-439f` (`addictive-snooty-wildcat`, open, P2) reports\n  the same `bridge_status` failure with a narrower scope. Linked `duplicates`. Its AC1-AC5\n  are a strict subset of this ticket's ACs and will be satisfied by the same fix. cca6 also\n  independently names the correct resolver, `_engine_support/reads.py:100-120`.\n- **0(b) reported-against floor:** `269f7b49c44f` — i.e. the report is against current\n  `origin/main`. No suspect-path movement to account for.\n- **0(c) worktree:** `269f7b49c44f` (= `origin/main`), current.\n\n### Proven root cause\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py:89`\n\n    path = repo_root / \".tickets-tracker\" / \".env-id\"\n\nand its sibling constant at `last_pass.py:35`\n\n    DETAIL_RELATIVE = Path(\".tickets-tracker/.bridge_state/last-pass.json\")\n\njoined at `last_pass.py:170` and `:268` (`repo_root / DETAIL_RELATIVE`).\n\nThe caller `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py:288` passes `root = Path(config.repo_root(repo_root))` — the\n**repo root**, never the resolved tracker. `last_pass.snapshot()` then composes the store path\nfrom the hardcoded literal, so the `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` override and an absolute `tracker.dir`\nare both ignored on this path.\n\n### Discriminating experiment (runtime, not static)\nBuilt a real repo, ran `rebar init`, then **relocated** the store outside the repo root and set\n`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` to it — the deployed server's exact configuration. Two arms, same env:\n\n    [control] `rebar list`          rc=0   store readable through the resolver\n    [subject] `rebar bridge status` rc=1\n      Error: cannot read bridge status: cannot read local environment id from\n      <repo>/.tickets-tracker/.env-id: [Errno 2] No such file or directory\n\n    mentions repo_root/.tickets-tracker (the WRONG path)? True\n    mentions the CONFIGURED path?                        False\n\nThe control arm is what makes this discriminating: with the *same* `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`, the\nsame store, and the same repo, a resolver-honouring read succeeds. That rules out a broken\nstore, a wrong env var, and a failed relocation — the only surviving explanation is that this\none code path does not consult the resolver. Reproduces the live-server report exactly.\n\n### Defect attribution — `caused_by` = `b69c-5787-81b8-4052` (`antivirus-talkative-beauceron`)\nIntroducing commit `fe5a447061cde` (\"Add durable bridge status and canary witness\",\n`rebar-ticket: b69c-5787-81b8-4052`), which created `last_pass.py` carrying both hardcoded\nsites. Blame run with `-w -C -M` so a reformat/move carrier could not stand in for the origin.\n\n**Date test applied, and it clears the unmet-obligation reading.** `git show fe5a447^:src/rebar/config.py`\nshows `config.tracker_dir()` already present at the commit's **parent**, with the relocation\ncontract stated verbatim (\"`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` wins verbatim\"; \"an absolute value relocates the\nstore (EV-3b)\"). The obligation therefore predated the code by which it was ignored: this is not\na consumer that fell behind a later contract, it is a new store-path composition written past an\nexisting, documented resolver. Close class `plan_defect` rather than `regression` — nothing broke\na working behaviour; the site was born bypassing the seam.\n\n### Legitimacy: `defect` (auto-fix unlocked)\nCited authority: `src/rebar/config.py:138-156` documents relocation as a supported configuration\n(EV-3b), and `_engine_support/reads.py:100-120` implements the same contract for the read path.\nThe behaviour diverges from rebar's own documented contract, not merely from the reporter's\nexpectation.\n\n### Prior art discovered — an existing, UNENFORCED marker convention\n`# tickets-boundary-ok` is already documented (`docs/architecture.md:325-341`, and contrasted\nagainst `# raw-git-ok` in `scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py:70-100`) as sanctioning\n\"boundary-crossing *reads/layout* knowledge of `.tickets-tracker`\". Eleven sites already carry\nit. **Nothing enforces it** — no script in `scripts/`, no `make lint` step. AC4's gate should\ntherefore enforce the convention the repo already has rather than invent a second vocabulary.\n\nProceeding to the Step 7 sibling triage (77 occurrences) before Phase 2, since the root cause is\na repeatable pattern and the class — not just this instance — is the declared scope."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787859117405536339,"uuid":"e99d8f79-077c-41e5-b011-ce368c2e1836"}